  "notes": "Normative spec PRs (whatwg/html #10995, whatwg/dom #1353) are OPEN as of 2026-07-28 — Chrome 152 ships ahead of the merged spec; prose follows the WICG explainer and Chromium IDL, and the pages say so in the warn-block and specifications table. BCD records every engine as flag-gated and has not recorded Chrome 152's enabled-by-default milestone (freshness gap, checked 2026-07-28); the compat tables show BCD verbatim plus a labelled interim note anchored to the authoritative chromestatus milestone=152 listing. aria-owns forwarding is excluded from the shipping surface: ShadowRootReferenceTargetAriaOwns has no status field in runtime_enabled_features.json5 and is documented as a caveat (WICG/webcomponents #1091). Phase 2 (referenceTargetMap, exportid) is explicitly out of scope as not shipping; noted in the warn-block. WPT per-run pass counts could not be captured (wpt.fyi summary endpoint returned empty results for the Chrome 152 run at fetch time); the tree of 15 tentative files is cited without counts. No chrome-platform-showcase concept route exists for this feature (feature index 200; label-for/aria-labelledby/basics 404) — pages link to the showcase instead of embedding an iframe, per the Case B contract."
